  "notes": "The native Japanese reading is {三|みっ}つ (mittsu) when counting things with the つ counter. In most other counter combinations, さん is used: ⟦{三|さん}{月|がつ}→さんがつ：00665⟧ (sangatsu, March), {三|さん}{本|ぼん} (sanbon, three long objects). Note how the counter {本|ほん} becomes ぼん after さん.",
